An elegant and optimal solution in C++ for **Maximum Total Beauty of the Gardens**.

### Method Explanation

1. **Definitions & Properties**:
   - A garden is **complete** if it has at least `target` flowers. Flowers cannot be removed, so any garden initially having `flowers[i] >= target` is already complete.
   - We cap each `flowers[i]` at `target` since having more flowers does not provide any extra benefit.
   - We sort `flowers` in non-decreasing order.
   - If we decide to make $k$ gardens complete ($0 \le k \le n$), we should greedily pick the largest $k$ gardens (i.e., indices from $n-k$ to $n-1$). Any garden initially having $\ge target$ flowers must be among these complete gardens.

2. **Iterating over $k$**:
   - We iterate $k$ from $0$ to $n$.
   - The cost to make the suffix of length $k$ complete is $\sum_{i=n-k}^{n-1} (\text{target} - \text{flowers}[i])$.
   - If this cost exceeds `newFlowers`, we cannot choose this or any larger $k$.
   - With the remaining flowers `left = newFlowers - cost`:
     - If $k = n$ (all gardens complete), the beauty is simply $n \times \text{full}$.
     - If $k < n$ (there are $m = n - k$ incomplete gardens), we want to maximize the minimum number of flowers $x \in [\text{flowers}[0], \text{target} - 1]$ among the remaining $m$ gardens.
     - Because the cost to raise the prefix to at least $x$ is monotonically non-decreasing with $x$, we can binary search for the optimal $x \le \text{target} - 1$.
     - Total beauty for a valid $(k, x)$ is $k \times \text{full} + x \times \text{partial}$.

3. **Complexity**:
   - Sorting takes $O(n \log n)$.
   - For each of the $O(n)$ choices of $k$, binary search takes $O(\log(\text{target}))$.
   - Total time complexity is $O(n \log n + n \log(\text{target}))$, which easily runs well within the 2-second time limit for $n, \text{target} \le 10^5$.
   - Space complexity is $O(n)$ for prefix sums.

### C++ Source Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    long long maximumBeauty(vector<int>& flowers, long long newFlowers, int target, int full, int partial) {
        int n = flowers.size();

        // Cap flowers at target
        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
            if (flowers[i] > target) {
                flowers[i] = target;
            }
        }

        sort(flowers.begin(), flowers.end());

        // Prefix sums to quickly calculate cost of raising gardens to a certain level
        vector<long long> pref(n + 1, 0);
        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
            pref[i + 1] = pref[i] + flowers[i];
        }

        // Suffix cost to make gardens [i...n-1] complete
        // cost_complete[k] = cost to make top k gardens complete
        vector<long long> cost_complete(n + 1, 0);
        for (int k = 1; k <= n; ++k) {
            cost_complete[k] = cost_complete[k - 1] + (target - flowers[n - k]);
        }

        long long max_beauty = 0;

        for (int k = 0; k <= n; ++k) {
            long long cost = cost_complete[k];
            if (cost > newFlowers) {
                break;
            }

            int m = n - k; // number of incomplete gardens
            if (m == 0) {
                max_beauty = max(max_beauty, 1LL * n * full);
                continue;
            }

            // Gardens in 0..m-1 must have flowers < target.
            // If the largest one is already target, it cannot be considered incomplete.
            if (flowers[m - 1] == target) {
                continue;
            }

            long long left = newFlowers - cost;
            long long low = flowers[0], high = target - 1;
            long long best_x = flowers[0];

            while (low <= high) {
                long long mid = low + (high - low) / 2;
                // Find how many gardens in 0..m-1 have < mid flowers
                auto it = upper_bound(flowers.begin(), flowers.begin() + m, mid);
                int p = it - flowers.begin();
                long long needed = 1LL * p * mid - pref[p];

                if (needed <= left) {
                    best_x = mid;
                    low = mid + 1;
                } else {
                    high = mid - 1;
                }
            }

            long long current_beauty = 1LL * k * full + 1LL * best_x * partial;
            max_beauty = max(max_beauty, current_beauty);
        }

        return max_beauty;
    }
};
```

