An efficient way to solve this problem is using Dijkstra's algorithm. 

We can define our state as `(cost, time, u)`, representing arriving at city `u` with a total accumulated passing fee `cost` and elapsed time `time`. Since we want to find the path that minimizes the total cost, we can use a min-heap ordered by `cost`.

To avoid redundant computations and prune states, we maintain an array `min_time[u]` which stores the minimum time seen so far to reach city `u`. When extracting a state `(cost, time, u)`:
- Because states are popped in non-decreasing order of cost, if we encounter city `u` with `time >= min_time[u]`, this state has both a greater/equal cost and a greater/equal time compared to an earlier state, so it is strictly dominated and can be discarded.
- Otherwise, we update `min_time[u] = time` and relax all outgoing edges to its neighbors.

The first time we pop destination city `n - 1`, the cost is guaranteed to be minimal. If the priority queue empties without reaching `n - 1`, it is impossible to reach within `maxTime`, and we return `-1`.

### C++ Source Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int minCost(int maxTime, vector<vector<int>>& edges, vector<int>& passingFees) {
        int n = passingFees.size();
        vector<vector<pair<int, int>>> adj(n);
        for (const auto& edge : edges) {
            int u = edge[0], v = edge[1], time = edge[2];
            adj[u].push_back({v, time});
            adj[v].push_back({u, time});
        }

        // min_time[u] stores the minimum time taken to reach node u so far
        vector<int> min_time(n, maxTime + 1);

        // Min-heap stores tuples of (cost, time, city)
        priority_queue<tuple<int, int, int>, vector<tuple<int, int, int>>, greater<tuple<int, int, int>>> pq;
        pq.push({passingFees[0], 0, 0});

        while (!pq.empty()) {
            auto [cost, time, u] = pq.top();
            pq.pop();

            // If we arrived at city u with an equal or worse time, prune this branch
            if (time >= min_time[u]) {
                continue;
            }
            min_time[u] = time;

            if (u == n - 1) {
                return cost;
            }

            for (const auto& [v, travelTime] : adj[u]) {
                int nextTime = time + travelTime;
                int nextCost = cost + passingFees[v];

                if (nextTime <= maxTime && nextTime < min_time[v]) {
                    pq.push({nextCost, nextTime, v});
                }
            }
        }

        return -1;
    }
};
```

